.\" Man page for obs (Obsidian CLI Ops)
.\" Updated: 2026-06-26
.TH OBS 1 "2026-06-26" "obsidian-cli-ops 4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obs \- manage Obsidian vaults with AI\-powered knowledge\-graph analysis
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obs
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIarguments\fR]
.br
.B obs ai
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B obs
(Obsidian CLI Ops) is a command\-line tool for managing one or more
Obsidian vaults, analyzing their knowledge graph, and applying optional
AI assistance over notes and links.
.PP
A thin ZSH launcher (\fBobs.zsh\fR) dispatches to a Python core. The launcher
resolves a Python interpreter that has the required dependencies, in priority
order: an explicit
.BR OBS_PYTHON ,
an install.sh\-provisioned user venv
.RI ( ~/.local/share/obs/venv ),
the Homebrew formula venv
.RI ( libexec/venv ),
and finally the ambient
.B python3
(with a warning, since its dependencies may be missing).
.PP
When called without a command,
.B obs
lists the known vaults (equivalent to \fBobs vaults\fR).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-v
Enable verbose output. May be given before the command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Primary
.TP
.B (none)\fR, \fBvaults
List all known vaults from the database.
.TP
.B stats\fR [\fIvault\fR]
Show statistics. With a vault name or ID, show that vault's statistics;
with no argument, show overall statistics across vaults.
.TP
.B discover\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-scan\fR]
Find Obsidian vaults under
.IR path
(defaults to the current directory). With
.BR \-\-scan ,
perform a deeper scan.
.TP
.B scan\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-analyze\fR] [\fB\-\-prune\fR | \fB\-\-no\-prune\fR]
Scan a vault directory and register or update it in the database. The default
is additive: notes are added and updated but never removed, so a note deleted
or renamed on disk lingers in the index. With
.BR \-\-prune ,
sweep rows whose file is gone from disk (cascading to their links, tags, graph
metrics, and embeddings); the sweep is skipped with a warning if the scan sees
zero files, guarding against wiping the index on a mis\-pointed path.
.BR \-\-no\-prune
is the explicit default. Unchanged notes are skipped by content\-hash
comparison, preserving the AI embedding cache. With
.BR \-\-analyze ,
run graph analysis immediately after scanning.
.SS Vault Management
.TP
.B vault info\fR \fIvault\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show metadata for a single vault: name, ID, path, note count, last-scanned
and registration times. Accepts a vault name or ID prefix.
.TP
.B vault rename\fR \fIvault\fR \fInew\-name\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Change a vault's display name. The path and ID are unchanged. A rename that
would collide with another vault's name is refused.
.TP
.B vault delete\fR \fIvault\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Remove a vault from the database. The vault folder on disk is never touched;
deletion cascades to the vault's notes, links, tags, and metrics. Without
.BR \-\-force ,
print a dry-run preview only.
.SS Graph Analysis
.TP
.B analyze\fR \fIvault\fR
Analyze the vault's graph metrics (PageRank, centrality, clustering,
orphan and hub detection). Accepts a vault name or ID prefix.
.TP
.B health\fR \fIvault\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show a vault health dashboard scoring four dimensions (connectivity,
link integrity, structure, freshness) with recommendations. With
.BR \-\-json ,
emit machine\-readable output.
.SS AI Features
AI features require a configured provider (Gemini API, Anthropic API,
Gemini CLI, Claude CLI, or Ollama). Run \fBobs ai setup\fR first.
.TP
.B ai status
Show AI provider status.
.TP
.B ai setup
Run the interactive AI setup wizard.
.TP
.B ai test\fR [\fB\-\-provider\fR \fIname\fR]
Test all configured AI providers, or only the named provider.
.TP
.B ai similar\fR \fInote\fR
Find notes similar to the given note ID.
.TP
.B ai analyze\fR \fInote\fR
Analyze a note with AI.
.TP
.B ai duplicates\fR \fIvault\fR
Find duplicate notes within a vault.
.TP
.B ai suggest\-links\fR \fInote\fR
Suggest new links for a note.
.TP
.B ai gaps\fR \fIvault\fR
Find knowledge gaps in a vault.
.TP
.B ai summarize\fR \fIvault\fR
Summarize a vault's themes.
.TP
.B ai refactor\fR \fIvault\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Propose an AI\-powered reorganization of a vault. With
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
preview without applying.
.TP
.B ai merge\-suggest\fR \fIvault\fR [\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-provider\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Find candidate notes to merge.
.TP
.B ai tag\-suggest\fR \fItarget\fR [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-confidence\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Suggest tags for a vault or a single note. With
.BR \-\-apply ,
write the suggested tags.
.I target
may be a vault name/ID or a note ID.
.TP
.B ai quality\fR \fItarget\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Score a vault or note on quality dimensions.
.I target
may be a vault name/ID or a note ID.
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B doctor\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIid\fR] [\fB\-\-layer\fR \fIlayer\fR]... [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Run self\-diagnostic checks across seven layers:
.BR python " (runtime & imports),"
.BR database " (SQLite integrity & vault count),"
.BR vault " (path, freshness, note/link counts),"
.BR sync " (vault\-vs\-index drift: ghosts, missing, scan errors),"
.BR mcp " (Claude Desktop config),"
.BR docs " (doc count accuracy),"
and
.BR icloud " (macOS write\-latency & offload detection)."
Use
.B \-\-layer
(repeatable) to restrict to a subset.
Exits 0 when all checks pass/warn; 1 on any fail; 2 on unexpected error.
.SS Board Management
.TP
.B board refresh\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Refresh the \fI_ACTION\-BOARD.md\fR file from atlas project state, vault stats,
and \fI.STATUS\fR files. Defaults to the first research vault; use
.B \-\-all
to update all vaults and
.B \-\-dry\-run
to preview without writing.
.TP
.B board status\fR [\fB\-\-vault\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show whether the board file exists, when it was last refreshed, and whether
the vault has ghost drift. Defaults to all vaults.
.SS Utilities
.TP
.B help\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR]
Show help. With
.BR \-\-all ,
list every command.
.TP
.B version
Show the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OBS_PYTHON
Path to the Python interpreter used to run the core. Overrides automatic
resolution; must point to an interpreter that has obs's dependencies.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disable colored output. Color is also disabled when standard
output is not a terminal.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for the install.sh\-provisioned user venv. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share ,
so the venv lives at
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/obs/venv .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/obs/obsidian_vaults.db
Knowledge\-graph database (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.config/obs/last_vault
Last\-used vault ID.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Mobile Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents
Default Obsidian root searched on macOS (iCloud).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List vaults:
.B obs
.TP
Show statistics for a vault:
.B obs stats my\-vault
.TP
Discover vaults under a directory:
.B obs discover ~/Notes
.TP
Analyze a vault's graph:
.B obs analyze my\-vault
.TP
Check vault health as JSON:
.B obs health my\-vault \-\-json
.TP
Inspect a single vault's metadata:
.B obs vault info my\-vault
.TP
Rename a vault's display name:
.B obs vault rename my\-vault "My Vault"
.TP
Preview a vault deletion, then commit it:
.B obs vault delete my\-vault
.br
.B obs vault delete my\-vault \-\-force
.TP
Configure and test AI providers:
.B obs ai setup
.br
.B obs ai test
.TP
Refresh the research action board:
.B obs board refresh
.TP
Check board refresh status:
.B obs board status
.TP
Preview an AI refactor without applying it:
.B obs ai refactor my\-vault \-\-dry\-run
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B obs
exits
.B 0
on success and non\-zero on error (for example, a missing required
argument or an unresolved Python interpreter).
